# Booking copy must not break the flow

A wording change is still a code change. Vite builds without checking that every name exists, so a missing import or ref ships and crashes only when that screen renders.

## When editing visible text

- Change the string only. Leave imports, hooks, refs, and the surrounding JSX in place.
- Do not drop an import while a call to that function remains.
- Do not remove `useRef` / `useState` while the component still uses that binding.

```tsx
// ❌ wording edit also deleted the import
<span>{formatCertificateTerm(months)}</span>

// ✅ same sentence, call still wired
<span>не ограничен</span>
```

## Before a production build

Run the certificate screen tests and stop if they fail:

```
pnpm exec vitest run src/widgets/booking/certificate
```

Those tests open the pick step and the buyer summary for both electronic and paper certificates. A `ReferenceError` there means the main flow is broken.
